M1 VERDICT (honest)
==============================================================================
  Local-before-Hubble AND sub-floor window in Σ0: 1e-06 … 1e+00
  ⇒ F-A4 is PASS-SHAPED on the scale clock: exit *can* precede Hubble exit
    and can occur before the CSW floor for isotropy-to-structure seeds.

  Caveats (load-bearing, not fine print):
  1. Pure-radiation H(a) near exit is an approximation; full multi-fluid
     contraction shifts a_loc by O(1) factors, not 30 orders.
  2. Σ0 is a homogeneous Bianchi seed. Real collapse is inhomogeneous;
     overdense patches can reach large local σ earlier (helps RP-A locally).
  3. MIXMASTER-WINDOW: classical GR can go chaotic (Σ≳1, R_σ≫ξ) *before*
     the medium cutoff. RP-A needs either to survive that window or to
     redefine exit by a different curvature invariant. NOT computed here.
  4. This does NOT write F-A1–F-A3 matching. M1 only prices the shear clock.
  5. Grade: reconstructed milestone, not a derived bounce.
